    "Op_catd(E) acts over CoAt2(K). Its whole Hom action has T(Hom_K(x,y)) as input; the corrected diagnostic still factors through the ordinary hom action of op and CoAt2(E). The old untransposed input is explicitly rejected.",
    "Functor_catd action uses Cartesian fibre-Homs and its actual Unit_prof(Cat_cart) projection. Ordinary ambient Hom object action and Op noncollapse remain checked.",
    "Positive mixed postmaps and recursively compiled F/G retain general lax Functord inputs. The negative source slot uses the existing StrictTransfor classifier required by Functor_catd_func; public Functord is not redefined.",
    "Product distribution and constant-middle composition retain the original transparent products, generic lax FF/GG, whole/capped actions, object/inner-arrow computations and intrinsic-cell typing. Higher helpers expose canonical Hom results.",
    "Hom_catd and Transf_catd use negative sections in TotalOp_catd(E) over R(K); their fibre and constant-family comparisons use the current Cartesian Hom and native TotalOp_func conversion."
  ],
